{"abstract":[{"text":"Drastically reduce RAM footprint and accelerate matrix-vector products using Compressed Sparse Row (CSR) and Column (CSC) formats.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sparse Data Types","anchor":"Sparse-Data-Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/SparseMatrix","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/SparseFormat"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftpreprocessing\/sparsedatastructures"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/SparseDataStructures","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High-dimensional data transformations—including one-hot categorical encodings, n-gram bags of words, TF-IDF vectors, and interaction graphs—typically yield matrices where 95% to 99.9% of entries are zeros."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storing such datasets as dense arrays requires gigabytes of memory and burns CPU cycles iterating over zeros. "},{"code":"SparseMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implements Compressed Sparse Row (CSR) and Compressed Sparse Column (CSC) compression formats, reducing memory consumption by 10x–50x."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Storage Formats","anchor":"Storage-Formats","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"text":"Compressed Sparse Row (CSR)","anchor":"Compressed-Sparse-Row-CSR","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stores non-zero values row-by-row:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Non-zero numerical entries.","type":"tex