"type":"text","text":"These routines utilize SIMD hardware instructions on Apple Silicon CPUs, delivering maximum throughput."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage","type":"heading"},{"code":["import SwiftPreprocessing","","\/\/ 1. Create a sparse matrix from a dense array","let dense: [[Double]] = [","    [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],","    [0.0, 2.0, 0.0],","    [0.0, 0.0, 3.0]","]","let sparse = SparseMatrix(dense: dense, format: .csr)","print(\"Sparsity: \\(sparse.sparsity)\") \/\/ ~ 0.667","","\/\/ 2. Accelerated matrix-vector product","let x = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]","let y = try sparse.multiply(vector: x)","print(y) \/\/ [1.0, 4.0, 9.0]","","\/\/ 3. Matrix Transpose & CSC conversion","let csc = sparse.toCSC()","let transposed = sparse.transpose()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftPreprocessing"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Memory-Efficient Sparse Matrix Representations"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/FeatureScaling","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/EncodersAndImputers"],"generated":true}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://SwiftPreprocessing/documentation/SwiftPreprocessing/SparseMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftpreprocessing\/sparsematrix","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/SparseMatrix","title":"SparseMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SparseMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Memory-efficient sparse matrix storage implementing Compressed Sparse Row (CSR) and Column (CSC) formats.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SparseMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftPreprocessing/documentation/SwiftPreprocessin